engine-pick-empty = `{ $command }` of { $commit } would change nothing ({ $what }): no commit created, nothing in progress, nothing changed
engine-pick-sequencer = a sequence of several commits started from a terminal is in progress (`.git/sequencer`): `{ $command }` would leave it half done or would also undo the commits already made, nothing changed. Continue or abort it from a terminal (`git { $git } --continue`, `git { $git } --skip` or `git { $git } --abort`)
engine-pick-local-changes = there are local changes to tracked files ({ $files }): commit or stash them (`stash.push`) and retry `{ $command }` (no autostash); nothing changed
engine-pick-conflicts = there are conflicted files ({ $files }): resolve them before `{ $command }`; nothing changed
engine-pick-mainline-range = `mainline` must be between 1 and { $n } (the parents of { $commit }), not { $m }
engine-pick-mainline-needed = { $commit } is a merge commit with { $n } parents: give with `mainline` (from 1 to { $n }) the parent to take the changes against (usually 1, the branch that was merged into)
engine-pick-mainline-not-merge = `mainline` applies only to a merge commit, and { $commit } is not one
engine-pick-already-applied = its changes are already in the branch
engine-pick-already-reverted = its changes are not (or no longer) in the branch
engine-pick-overwrite = `{ $command }` would overwrite local changes or untracked files ({ $files }): commit, stash or move them and try again; nothing changed
engine-pick-head-moved = HEAD changed while `{ $command }` was being prepared: nothing changed, try again
engine-pick-continue-empty = after the resolution the result is the same as HEAD: nothing to commit; to get out use `{ $abort }`
engine-pick-no-message = git did not prepare a message (`MERGE_MSG`) and the incoming commit cannot be read: give `message` and repeat `{ $id }`; nothing committed
engine-pick-continue-conflicts = conflicted files remain ({ $files }): resolve them and stage them (`index.stage`), then repeat `{ $id }`; nothing committed
engine-pick-detached = HEAD is detached: `{ $id }` must be done on a branch, nothing changed. Switch to a branch (`branch.checkout`) or create one here (`branch.create`) and try again
engine-pick-unborn = branch `{ $name }` has no commits yet: `{ $id }` needs a commit to apply on, nothing changed
engine-pick-rev-empty = `rev` must be a commit id, a branch or a tag, not empty
engine-pick-skip-failed = `{ $command }` of { $commit } would change nothing, but `git { $git } --skip` did not close the operation ({ $stderr }): reload the status; the branch as it was is in `{ $backup }`
engine-pick-branch-not-moved = `git { $git }` finished without errors but `{ $full }` did not move ({ $text }): check index and worktree; the branch as it was is in `{ $backup }`
engine-pick-branch-gone = after `{ $id }`, `{ $full }` no longer exists
engine-pick-head-moved-id = HEAD changed while `{ $id }` was being prepared: nothing changed, try again
engine-pick-backup-kept = the branch as it was is in `{ $backup }`
engine-pick-unexpected-result = the branch is at { $after } but it is not the expected result of `{ $command }` (did a hook or another process move it?): the operation does not go in the journal, the branch as it was is in `{ $backup }`
